    "md5": "8e1532d39735d340d28c81f5192630d6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1935,
    "chunk_text": "With that being said, now, I would like to take up the matter of the salinity barrier. As the Minister of Water Supply and Estate Infrastructure Development, I must say that the salinity barrier had been constructed across the Nilwala River in Weragampita area with the aim of providing uninterrupted clean drinking water to approximately 800,000 people in parts of Matara and Hambantota Districts; that was the notion with which that barrier was built. The Hon. Buddhika Pathirana brought this issue to my attention and we had multiple meetings.\n\nI would like to remind this House that when I became the Minister of Water Supply and Estate Infrastructure Development in 2023, I inherited this issue. From the time I have taken over this Ministry, we have been trying to look for a collective solution. However, we do not wish to make this into a circus; we are trying to see how we can come up with a solution. During the period of construction of this salinity barrier, a substantial portion of the river was covered by the cofferdam, impacting on about seven planting seasons. However, following the completion of the construction in September, 2022, farmers had been able to carry out their agricultural activities without flood threats during the Maha season in\n\n105 106\n\n\u0db4\u0db4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2 )\u0dca\u0dd4\u0daf\n\n2020/2023 and the Y ala season in 2023. Nevertheless, during the last four months of 2023, a heavy rainfall led to significant flooding of agricultural lands. This flood condition impacted not only on the Nilwala River Basin, but also on other areas. Furthermore, the flood at the end of May, 2024, receded within four to five days, similar to the flood in 2017 before the construction of the salinity barrier.\n\nIn response to farmers\u2019 protests claiming that the construction of the salinity barrier caused the flooding of paddy lands along the Nilwala River in late 2023, an investigation is ongoing to determine its impact."
  },
