    "chunk_text": "At the same time, I feel the need to address certain other statements that were made in this House. When my Colleague, the Hon. Premnath C. Dolawatte was speaking about the Bangladesh issue, I think he was merely trying to instill the fact that nearly two years ago, we were also not far away from the situation that has errupted in Bangladesh today. That must be taken into account and I think, as a Member of this House, he is within his rights to speak about that. Nobody from the Opposition, be it the Chief Opposition Whip or the Leader of the Opposition, could say that this is what you should talk on and what you should not talk on. Then, why did we speak about the \u201cSakwala\u201d programme and why did we speak about Bangladesh? At the end of the day, we are here in this House to do justice to the mandate that has been given to us. Right after the crisis, there were Members from all parties in the Opposition who, at different points of time, always said, \u201cNo, we will not be able to come out of this crisis; this country is going to rot even further; the queues will continue; there is not going to be diesel, petrol or gasoline and there is going to be so many other issues\". But, the Government made sure that we recovered. Then, on the road to recovery, when we spoke about debt restructuring, at that particular point also, the same voices which were so sceptical about our recovery were sceptical about signing the Debt Restructuring Agreement, too, but still, we got that done.\n\nToday, this situation has erupted in Bangladesh. I think every Hon. Member in this House and every person in this country must acknowledge the fact that one wrong\n\n\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0bc6\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0