    "chunk_size_bytes": 1682,
    "chunk_text": "By the proposed Amendment, the accused person and the prosecution enter into an agreement, where the accused would plead guilty instead of going to trial, in consequence of which there may be reduced charges and recommendation for a lower sentence, fine or restitution amount. By the proposed Amendment, it is also expected to resolve the criminal cases in an effective manner, where lower sentences tied to plea agreement would also address prison overcrowding.\n\nsafeguards in this law to protect the rights of the accused also. However, if the accused, at one point in time, wants to plead guilty because he knows whether he has committed the crime or not and shorten his term, he should also be given some sort of an inducement or encouragement to do so without wasting time of the court and the prosecutor and public money so that more important matters could be taken up by the court. That is an accepted system and I think it will open up a new chapter in the Sri Lankan criminal justice system. I hope that would work well and address prison overcrowding and clear the backlog of cases in courts. So, that is the reason behind bring in this Code of Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Bill.\n\nI must also say that we are proposing two Amendments to this Bill at the Committee Stage as there were some concerns expressed by the Sectoral Oversight Committee as well as by some lawyers that if you leave the whole thing without any indication to the judge, since the judge is not bound by the agreement entered into or the suggestion made both by the accused and the prosecutor, and if the judge disregards the whole thing and gives a higher sentence, the accused could be prejudiced."
  },
