    "chunk_text": "incorporating those amendments and looking into the Bills at their different stages and also the Legal Draftsman\u2019s Department for cooperating with us in incorporate those amendments. We know that when you draft a law, it goes up and down and that it is not an easy task. Therefore, I thought it fit to mention them here and thank them: the Subcommittee members, the Ministry Officials, the Legal Draftsman, the Attorney-General, and all those who got involved in drafting these laws and submitting them for the betterment of our country.\n\nlanguage and culture; they respect each other and is like a platform which allows everybody to move on. I am extremely grateful that in this year's Presidential Election, nobody is taking notice of race, religion or language; people are talking about national issues. Some people are trying to twist all that and take advantage, but people are ignoring it. People want someone who can drive this country forward, develop this nation and who can give a better level of life for everyone while creating a safe and secure future.\n\nIt is a good step. I think we should build on that and not go backward on that. I know, some people will lose out on it because no longer, their divisive agenda is sellable and they are upset about it. But, as a country, we should be proud that people are coming together and are talking about national issues and not about racial, ethnic or other artificial issues which have divided us for such a long period of time.\n\nSir, I am also grateful that at the Committee on Parliamentary Business, we have agreed to pass these good laws without a Division. And, we will continue to come up with such other laws. Law is a process which continues to evolve. You need to have standing committees looking into all these laws because no law is perfect. If you wait for a perfect law to come, it would never come."
