    "chunk_index": 150,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "0d1f6b7e2528432c15c7b9db5a5adc22",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1422,
    "chunk_text": "First time and then, there were two petitioners who went to the Supreme Court on that. They cited me as a respondent and I appeared in person. Then, the Supreme Court gave its Determination stating that subject to the change of wording the Supreme Court itself suggested, it could be passed with a simple majority.\n\nThe Central Working Committee of the Ilankai Tamil Arasu Kadchi met two days ago, on Sunday, the 01st of September in Vavuniya and after a long deliberation of five hours - that was the fifth meeting at which we were considering these matters - we took a definite decision not to support the so-called Tamil common candidate. Ours is the only Tamil party which has taken that courageous decision not to support the so-called Tamil common candidate. We have been branded traitors, we have been called names, but for the sake of our people and for the sake of the country, we took that courageous decision with an overwhelming majority. Then, at the end of the meeting, before the resolution was passed, those who dissented were asked and they said, \u201cNo, we do not need a vote. It can be accepted.\u201d So, it was accepted wholeheartedly without a division. That is what our\n\nCentral Committee decided. When we took that decision, we also took a decision that, as a responsible political party, which is the main Tamil political party, it is our bounden duty to inform our people as to whom they should vote."
  },
